{
  "_comment": [
    "FIXTURES DE PARIDADE TREINO<->SERVING",
    "",
    "Cada caso define uma entrada canonica (input) e o vetor de features esperado",
    "(expected_vector_computed). TANTO a implementacao Go (internal/ranker, J1) QUANTO a",
    "Python (ml/features, J2) devem produzir o MESMO vetor para cada caso.",
    "",
    "TOLERANCIA (da spec feature_spec.yaml, parity_test_tolerance):",
    "  - float: abs(go_value - py_value) <= 1e-6",
    "    (o vetor e float32; ruido de cast float32->float64 e ~1.19e-7)",
    "  - int / bucket: igualdade exata",
    "",
    "VALORES GOLD: calculados pelo bootstrap Python (ml/features/python/test_parity_cases.py)",
    "em 2026-06-04 com feature_spec_version 1.0.0.",
    "",
    "HASH CANONICO: murmur3_32(value, seed, unsigned) % num_buckets",
    "  Python: mmh3.hash(value, seed, signed=False) % num_buckets",
    "  Go:     murmur3.SeedSum32(uint32(seed), []byte(value)) % uint32(num_buckets)",
    "",
    "COMO PLUGAR:",
    "  Go  (J1): TestParityFromFixtures em internal/ranker/parity_test.go —",
    "            le este arquivo, chama Featurize(input), compara expected_vector_computed.",
    "  Python (J2): test_parity_cases.py em ml/features/python/ —",
    "               le este arquivo, chama featurize(input), compara expected_vector_computed.",
    "",
    "ATUALIZACAO DE FIXTURES:",
    "  Ao alterar a spec (ver politica de versao em feature_spec.yaml), recalcular",
    "  os expected_vector_computed aqui e incrementar feature_spec_version.",
    "  Ambos os testes falham com fixture desatualizado — esse e o comportamento correto."
  ],
  "feature_spec_version": "1.0.0",
  "cases": [
